From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0817: shared memory uploads: d3d12_upload_census, d3d12_upload_merge (+ bridge pages), d3d12_upload_skip_same, d3d12_upload_verify, shared_memory_merge_upload_calls (Direct3D 12; native stream, uploads session)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (native stream; scratch/uploads/DESIGN.md, TESTPLAN.md). Written without a build or a run: checked
  with clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only (the SDK's Release flags) of graphics/shared_memory.cpp, d3d12/shared_memory.cpp and
  d3d12/command_processor.cpp (the units that include the changed headers); 0 errors, no warning on an added line. The pristine files
  are the series up to 0814 (0815 / 0816 touch none of these files but deferred_command_list.h, far from the added hunk); the patch
  applies to the tree with 0815 and 0816 applied (git apply --check).
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: The shared memory uploads (guest pages the CPU wrote, copied from an upload buffer into the shared memory buffer before the
  draws that read them) cost 0.36 - 0.45 ms of GPU time a frame at 3200x2000, 470 - 600 copies at ~0.76 us each: the cost follows the
  count of copies. All new cvars default to today's behaviour; with all off the upload code is the old code (UploadRangesPlain).
  1. d3d12_upload_census (bool): every 10 s `[upload-census]` lines, per frame: copies made, pieces (copies before joining), bytes,
     calls (hoisted / in place with no run / in place for a page a draw of the run had read), transitions to and from the copy
     destination state and hoisted run pairs, distinct pages, pages uploaded more than once, pages uploaded in each of the last 2 / 8 /
     32 frames, hot pages, a histogram of the gaps between a frame's copies in address order and how many copies would be left if gaps
     of up to 0 / 4 / 16 / 64 KB were bridged, and how many pieces continue the one made before them; by request kind.
  2. d3d12_upload_merge (bool) + d3d12_upload_bridge_pages (0..64): the plan of a call is sorted with overlapping and touching runs
     made one; a copy that continues the one before it (the same upload buffer, the next bytes of it, the next bytes of the shared
     memory; the copy before it was recorded in the same call or, in a hoisted run, by an earlier call and is the last command of
     the hoisted stream) is made that copy, longer (DeferredCommandList::ExtendCopyBufferRegion). A gap of at most bridge_pages pages
     between two runs is copied with them when every page of it is valid, not GPU-written, not hot, and (in a hoisted run) no draw
     of the run has read it, so the copy writes the bytes the buffer already has. shared_memory_merge_upload_calls (bool, common
     code): a request with hot pages, on a backend with no byte path (this one), makes one UploadRanges call for its pages and its
     hot pages together, instead of two with the second one unsorted and a page that two asked ranges share copied twice.
  3. d3d12_upload_skip_same (0 off, 1 hot pages, 2 any page; d3d12_upload_skip_same_pages): a page at the start or end of a run of
     pages to upload whose bytes are the ones last copied to it (kept on this side: the copy is made from them, so they are what the
     buffer holds; let go at every transition of the buffer to the unordered access state and at ClearCache) is not copied again.
     A hot page is never valid nor watched, so nothing else changes; with 2 the plan's pages are made valid and watched first, as a
     copy does before its memcpy, and the pages left out stay so (a block that a guest write invalidated is needed again unchanged
     by the draws that read its other pages; the copy, the in-place transitions and the end of the hoisted run were for nothing).
  4. d3d12_upload_verify (bool, proof mode): the pages left out by 3 and the gap pages of 2 are read back from the buffer in place
     before the call's copies, and compared with the bytes expected when the submission is done; `[upload-verify] MISMATCH`.
Bucket: REDO

0817-shared-memory-upload-merge.patch (mcla-x86 native stream, uploads session).
---
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/deferred_command_list.h b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/deferred_command_list.h
index 5851ff6..1b55b39 100644
--- a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/deferred_command_list.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/deferred_command_list.h
@@ -163,6 +163,40 @@ class DeferredCommandList {
     args.num_bytes = num_bytes;
   }
 
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0817): upload_merge. D3DCopyBufferRegion, giving back where the arguments of the command are in
+  // the stream written to now (the main one, or the hoisted one after SetWritingHoisted(true)), for
+  // ExtendCopyBufferRegion.
+  size_t D3DCopyBufferRegionTracked(ID3D12Resource* dst_buffer, UINT64 dst_offset,
+                                    ID3D12Resource* src_buffer, UINT64 src_offset,
+                                    UINT64 num_bytes) {
+    auto& args = *reinterpret_cast<D3DCopyBufferRegionArguments*>(
+        WriteCommand(Command::kD3DCopyBufferRegion, sizeof(D3DCopyBufferRegionArguments)));
+    args.dst_buffer = dst_buffer;
+    args.dst_offset = dst_offset;
+    args.src_buffer = src_buffer;
+    args.src_offset = src_offset;
+    args.num_bytes = num_bytes;
+    return size_t(reinterpret_cast<const uintmax_t*>(&args) - write_stream_->data());
+  }
+  // Makes the copy at `args_index` of the hoisted or the main stream copy `extra_bytes` more (the bytes that follow its
+  // own in both buffers), if it is a copy and the last command of that stream: false (and nothing changed) if
+  // anything was written after it.
+  bool ExtendCopyBufferRegion(bool hoisted, size_t args_index, UINT64 extra_bytes) {
+    std::vector<uintmax_t>& stream = hoisted ? hoisted_stream_ : command_stream_;
+    constexpr size_t kArgumentElements =
+        (sizeof(D3DCopyBufferRegionArguments) + sizeof(uintmax_t) - 1) / sizeof(uintmax_t);
+    if (args_index < kCommandHeaderSizeElements || args_index + kArgumentElements != stream.size()) {
+      return false;
+    }
+    const CommandHeader& header =
+        *reinterpret_cast<const CommandHeader*>(stream.data() + (args_index - kCommandHeaderSizeElements));
+    if (header.command != Command::kD3DCopyBufferRegion) {
+      return false;
+    }
+    reinterpret_cast<D3DCopyBufferRegionArguments*>(stream.data() + args_index)->num_bytes += extra_bytes;
+    return true;
+  }
+
   void D3DCopyResource(ID3D12Resource* dst_resource, ID3D12Resource* src_resource) {
     auto& args = *reinterpret_cast<D3DCopyResourceArguments*>(
         WriteCommand(Command::kD3DCopyResource, sizeof(D3DCopyResourceArguments)));
